<!-- The Problem -->
<section class="product-section product-section--cream">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>College {{ lname }} recruiting shouldn&rsquo;t feel like guesswork.</h2>
    <p>Families spend thousands on showcases, club fees, and recruiting services, yet still can&rsquo;t answer the most basic question: <strong>where does my athlete actually fit?</strong></p>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-card">
        <h3>Rosters Are Scattered</h3>
        <p>Figuring out who&rsquo;s on a {{ lname }} team means visiting hundreds of college athletics sites one by one, copying rosters into a spreadsheet, and trying to make sense of it. Nobody has time for that.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <h3>No Real Analysis</h3>
        <p>Other tools list schools but don&rsquo;t analyze rosters. They can&rsquo;t tell you which programs have a depth gap at your athlete&rsquo;s {{ axis }}, who&rsquo;s graduating, or how your athlete compares to who&rsquo;s already there.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <h3>Expensive &amp; Shallow</h3>
        <p>Recruiting services charge hundreds for generic match lists any search could produce. Real {{ lname }} roster intelligence — the kind that actually informs decisions — hasn&rsquo;t existed anywhere else.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- What you'll actually see -->
<section class="product-section product-section--navy">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>What you&rsquo;ll actually see</h2>
    {% for para in sport.scenario %}
    <p style="max-width: 760px;{% if not loop.first %} margin-top: 16px;{% endif %}{% if loop.last %} font-size: 1.05em; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95);{% endif %}">{{ para | replace("'", "’") }}</p>
    {% endfor %}
    <p style="max-width: 760px; margin-top: 22px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">That&rsquo;s the difference between a list of school names and knowing <em>where the real opportunity is</em> — one picture per program, athletic and academic, built from every {{ lname }} roster so your family doesn&rsquo;t have to.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- What it analyzes -->
<section class="product-section product-section--white">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>What RosterWise&trade; {{ sport.name }} analyzes — at every program</h2>
    <p>It goes beyond school lists. RosterWise applies <a href="/roster-intelligence/" style="color: var(--gold-dark); font-weight: 600;">roster intelligence</a> — systematic analysis of who is actually on each {{ lname }} roster — across {{ sport.positionsExample }}.</p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Depth by {{ axis | title }}</h3>
        <p>See how every program is built by {{ axis }} — where a lineup spot is genuinely open versus stacked with returning starters.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Class-Year Gaps</h3>
        <p>Who {{ verb }} your athlete&rsquo;s {{ axis }}, and when do they graduate? A departing senior signals very different opportunity than a returning underclassman.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Physical Profile by {{ axis | title }}</h3>
        <p>How does each program build by {{ axis }}? See size and physical profiles so you know where your athlete aligns with the players already on the roster.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Geographic Recruiting Patterns</h3>
        <p>What states, regions, and countries does each program recruit from? Some recruit nationally; others draw heavily from specific areas. See the pattern behind every roster.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Pathway &amp; Club Analysis</h3>
        <p>What clubs, academies, and high schools did current players come from? Pathway data shows which pipelines each program draws from — and whether your athlete&rsquo;s background aligns.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Transfer Portal Activity</h3>
        <p>Does this program build through high-school recruiting or the transfer portal? A program&rsquo;s transfer pattern tells you how it fills spots — and what that means for a high-school recruit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>International Composition</h3>
        <p>What portion of the roster is domestic vs. international, and which countries are represented? This varies dramatically by division and conference — and shapes the landscape at each program.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Coach Tenure &amp; Direction</h3>
        <p>How long has the head coach been building this program? Stability tells you something about culture and direction. RosterWise includes coach tenure wherever available.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Academic Fit &amp; School Profile</h3>
        <p>It&rsquo;s not just athletics. See school size, academic strength, graduation rates, and setting for every program — so your athlete fits in the classroom, not just on the field.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>My RosterFit&trade; Personalized Scoring</h3>
        <p>Enter your athlete&rsquo;s profile — {{ axis }}, size, class year, GPA, test scores, geographic preferences — and RosterFit scores every program by how well they align with the actual roster. Not a generic match list. A personalized fit analysis built on real data.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Trust -->
<section class="product-section product-section--cream">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Built by a recruiting family, for yours.</h2>
    <div class="founder-section">
      <div class="founder-text">
        <p>RosterWise started with a question one recruiting parent asked another at a tournament: <em>&ldquo;How do you even figure out where your kid fits?&rdquo;</em></p>
        <p>The honest answer was: you don&rsquo;t. You visit hundreds of roster pages, take notes in a spreadsheet, and hope you&rsquo;re not missing something — or you pay a recruiting service hundreds of dollars for a list of schools you could have found yourself.</p>
        <p>We built the tool we couldn&rsquo;t find: one that goes deeper than school lists and actually analyzes rosters, surfaces opportunity, and gives families real intelligence to work with. No tool can predict recruiting outcomes — but the right data helps you ask better questions and focus your effort where it matters.</p>
        <p><strong>RosterWise is built by Grobe Games LLC.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

